Oreabetse:

Suggestion to not give player full information (they can go in cardinal directions), so that when a player goes into a room and leaves, if they go into a door in the same direction again, it's not guaranteed that they will end up in the same room. (i.e, the rooms are basically moving.). Basically, they could leave the kitchen and go to the hallway by going south, but if they go north again, they might end up in the bathroom again.

Basically using fnaf code logic to decide moving of the rooms. A number is assigned to each difficulty, depending on a random function that picks a number. If the random number is higher the number assigned to the difficulty, then the room will change. The higher difficulty is picked, the smaller the range of numbers the random function is scoped to, with a higher chance of the number being higher. The lower the difficulty, the higher the range of numbers the random function is scoped to, with a lower chance of the number being higher.
